<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul to aid China set up job training centre.</title>
<headline>Seoul to aid China set up job training centre.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea has agreed to help China set up a huge job training centre in Beijing by providing $10 million worth of equipment and printed materials, the domestic Yonhap news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>China's Labour Ministry plans to build the job training centre, capable of training about 121,400 people a year, in central Beijing by 1999, Yonhap said.</p>
<p>Investment by the Chinese government will amount to $8.54 million in land, construction and operating expenses, it said, quoting officials at Seoul's Labour Ministry.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
